---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Mark from "../components/Mark.astro";
---
<Base
  title="inixiative: technology for cooperation"
  description="Open building blocks, the agentic tools built from them that work the way you do, and designs for cooperation at scale."
  domain="inixiative"
>
  <script slot="head" is:inline>
    // Every primitive's GitHub homepage, and posts from before the rebuild, link to /#<repo>.
    // Those sections now live on their own pages; send the old anchors there.
    (function () {
      var id = location.hash.slice(1);
      if (!id) return;
      var blocks = ["primitives", "template", "json-rules", "permissions", "transitions", "prisma-map", "atlas", "rules-builder", "config", "gloss", "conditional-form", "hivemind"];
      var agentic = ["foundry", "agent-session", "archive", "signet", "kcp", "kingdom", "oracle", "bench"];
      var target = null;
      if (id === "think" || id === "governance") target = "/governance/";
      else if (id === "agentic") target = "/agentic/";
      else if (id === "building-blocks") target = "/building-blocks/";
      else if (id === "foundry-oracle") target = "/agentic/#oracle";
      else if (blocks.indexOf(id) !== -1) target = "/building-blocks/#" + id;
      else if (agentic.indexOf(id) !== -1) target = "/agentic/#" + id;
      if (target) location.replace(target);
    })();
  </script>

  <section class="hero">
    <span class="hero-mark"><Mark /></span>
    <h1 class="display-1">Technology for cooperation.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      inixiative builds open building blocks, the agentic tools built from them that keep your agents
      working the way you do, and designs for how people cooperate at scale.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="doors-title">
    <h2 id="doors-title" class="eyebrow" data-quiet>What we build</h2>
    <div class="card-grid doors">
      <a class="card" data-domain="building-blocks" href="/building-blocks/">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span>Building blocks</span>
        <h3>Stop rediscovering what you need to build.</h3>
        <p>A SaaS backend template you own, and the open libraries it is built from: rules, permissions, lifecycles and the tooling around them.</p>
        <p class="meta">template · json-rules · permissions · transitions</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" data-domain="agentic" href="/agentic/">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span>Agentic</span>
        <h3>An agent that works like you do.</h3>
        <p>Foundry is the workspace around your agent. With Kingdom, you decide who and what can reach your work. Archive keeps every session.</p>
        <p class="meta">Foundry · Kingdom · Archive · Signet · KCP</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" data-domain="governance" href="/governance/">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span>Governance</span>
        <h3>Designs for cooperation at scale.</h3>
        <p>The whitepaper and the proposals: how groups set rules, hold each other accountable, and invest together without a central referee.</p>
        <p class="meta">proposals · whitepaper · vocabulary</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-quiet>How it fits</span>
      <h2>The agentic tools are built on the building blocks, and both serve the governance work.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="layers">
      <div class="layer" data-domain="building-blocks">
        <span class="eyebrow">Building blocks</span>
        <p>Open libraries for rules, permissions and lifecycles, and a template that wires them into a working backend.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="layer-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="layer" data-domain="agentic">
        <span class="eyebrow">Agentic</span>
        <p>Foundry, Kingdom and Archive are built on those blocks. Foundry brings what you've decided into every agent session, and Kingdom lets you decide who and what can reach your work.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="layer-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="layer" data-domain="governance">
        <span class="eyebrow">Governance</span>
        <p>The design work it all serves: how groups set rules and cooperate at scale without a central referee.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" data-compact>
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        <strong>Most of it is open source.</strong> The building blocks, Archive, agent-session, Signet and KCP are MIT.
        Foundry is source-available. Kingdom and Oracle are closed.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="text-link" href="/open-source/">What's open and why</a>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/inixiative">github.com/inixiative</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
